  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7d518b92c0ea68e3f6accbd8146940140d4f098880cdad73330a6d2739ee2d13",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7d518b92c0ea-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts: \"We'll hear argument first this morning in Case 16-5294, McWilliams v. Dunn.\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7d518b92c0ea68e3f6accbd8146940140d4f098880cdad73330a6d2739ee2d13",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7d518b92c0ea-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer: \"WHERE, SOMEWHERE ELSE, DOES IT BECOME APPARENT THAT HE WANTS THE STATE TO APPOINT AN EXPERT? WHERE? I JUST WANT TO KNOW WHERE.\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7d518b92c0ea68e3f6accbd8146940140d4f098880cdad73330a6d2739ee2d13",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7d518b92c0ea-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, justice Kennedy: \"Suppose the Judge, the court, appoints the head of the psychiatric department at a distinguished private university, one person, and he comes in and he tells the defense counsel, now I'm going to explain to you what all these terms mean.\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7d518b92c0ea68e3f6accbd8146940140d4f098880cdad73330a6d2739ee2d13",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7d518b92c0ea-0001-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 30
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, justice Kagan: \"Sorry, General, but if we could just focus on -- because I think it would help to just sort of -- let's assume for the moment that this defendant did not get what he was asking for, which was a defense expert, and say whether Ake entitled him to such an expert.\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7d518b92c0ea68e3f6accbd8146940140d4f098880cdad73330a6d2739ee2d13",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7d518b92c0ea-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg: \"Is there any jurisdiction that holds that today, that all that Ake requires is a neutral expert? I thought by now every jurisdiction recognizes that Ake requires an expert who will be, essentially, part of the defense team.\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7d518b92c0ea68e3f6accbd8146940140d4f098880cdad73330a6d2739ee2d13",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7d518b92c0ea-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy: \"Well, if Ake says that you have a right to meaningful assistance from a psychiatrist, you, the defense, and then over time it becomes clear to us that that psychiatrist must be retained for the benefit of the defense only, is that a new clearly established holding, or is it simply a refinement of a clearly established right that was set forth in Ake?\""
      }
    ],
